// VEHICLE ASSEMBLY — the gantry you stack rockets in, and walk into.
//
// It used to be `hangar_roundA`: a sealed hexagonal dome with no way in (and
// 167 collider boxes when voxelised). This is an open assembly FRAME — you walk
// straight through it, which is what a building whose whole purpose is standing
// next to a rocket should let you do.
//
// The collider is the frame's own geometry, voxelised and merged into boxes, so
// the bars are solid and the bays between them are not. Regenerate it after any
// model/scale change; the boxes are in CENTRED MODEL units, so the node scale
// below applies to them exactly as it does to the mesh.
//
// Generated shell: 42 boxes, voxel cell 0.045 model units
// (1.00 x 1.00 x 1.00 model → 7.0 x 7.0 x 7.0 world; seat 3.500).
